OpenBounty <version>
====================

OpenBounty has been an open-source reimplementation of the 1990 strategy
game King's Bounty. The engine has shipped without game data; supply your
own asset pack.


INSTALL

  Linux:    extract the tarball and run ./openbounty
  Windows:  extract the zip and double-click openbounty.exe
  macOS:    extract the zip; Gatekeeper has blocked the first launch.
            Right-click openbounty in Finder, choose Open, then click
            Open in the dialog. Or, from a terminal:
              xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine ./openbounty


ASSET PACK

  OpenBounty has looked for a *.openbounty file in the directory you run
  it from, in your user data directory, and in an assets folder next to
  the binary. To create a pack from your own copy of the King's Bounty
  DOS distribution, run this in the directory that holds KB.EXE:

      ./openbounty --extract

  It has written kings-bounty.openbounty into your user data directory
  (Linux ~/.local/share/openbounty, macOS ~/Library/Application
  Support/OpenBounty, Windows %APPDATA%\OpenBounty), where the game
  finds it on the next launch.


CONTROLS

  Movement:   Arrow keys or numpad (8 directions on numpad)
  View army:  A         View character: V         Map: M
  Spells:     U         Contract:       I         Puzzle: P
  End week:   W         Search:         S
  Save+quit:  Q         Fast quit: Ctrl+Q
  Cheats:     start with --debug for a Debug page in the menu
  Exit menu:  Esc


